    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: d4f3145a7435258779630281032c31a33f4b78ca -->\nDelta review (merge of main only): **Needs changes before merge** (one blocker, from main's new per-setup post options).\n\n**The merge itself is fine.** `git diff upstream/main d4f3145a --stat` lists only this PR's 20 files; nothing from main was dropped. The `SetupPostOptionsDto` resolution is right: `smoothing: bool` with `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Not::not\")]` (absent = off), carried in both `from_options` and `into_options` (`crates/app/src/project/setup_options_dto.rs`), plus `smoothing: true` in the `own_post_options_round_trip_and_old_files_follow_the_document` assert (`crates/app/tests/setup_post_options.rs:200`).\n\n**Blocker: smoothing follows the active setup, but it is an operation-level effect.**\n- `crates/app/src/posting.rs:836`: `smoothing: if post_options(world).smoothing { ... }`. `post_options` is `setup_post_options::in_force` (posting.rs:216), the ACTIVE setup's options.\n- Main resolves `skip_stops` per operation from the operation's own setup (`posting.rs:748`: `setup_post_options::of(world, op.setup.as_deref()).skip_stops`). The module header (`crates/app/src/setup_post_options.rs:11-19`) puts operation-level effects there, and only Output (`per_op`) and `threading` in the program-level group.\n- `program_problems` (`setup_post_options.rs:64-92`) checks only `per_op` and `threading` (line ~85). It does not check `smoothing`, so a program whose setups disagree on smoothing is not refused.\n- Result: a setup that owns `smoothing = off` still gets smoothing words if the active setup has it on, and a setup that owns `smoothing = on` is silently ignored if the active one is off. Smoothing changes the cut path (within tolerance), and it is stated per op and reset at the op's end, exactly like skip. So the setup's explicit choice is ignored silently.\n\nRequested before merge:\n1. `posting.rs:836`: read the flag from the op's own setup, `crate::setup_post_options::of(world, op.setup.as_deref()).smoothing`, as line 748 does. Add a test with two setups, one on and one off, that checks each op's stream.\n2. Optional: update the `smoothing` doc comment in `schema.rs` and the `Smoothing` word in `options_value` (posting.rs:236), which stays the active setup's and is document-wide for scripts, so they say which level they are.\n\n**Local results** (merged with main; a delta only, shared target dir): `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test smoothing` 6 passed; `--test setup_post_options` 9 passed; `cargo test -p camcraft-post` all green (7, 3, 9, 3, 33); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. UI suites were not rerun (one-line change in `post_options.rs`, no logic from main touched).\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
