    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: ede835925093c9fbb37bd3042ef5eb92df860f62 -->\n**Review of the fix since d4f3145a (M3, independent of the author): Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\n**The fix (ede83592):** `op_streams` now gates each operation's smoothing ask on `setup_post_options::of(world, op.setup.as_deref()).smoothing`, which is the operation's own setup, read the same way `skip_stops` is read at `posting.rs:748`. This resolves the earlier blocker.\n\n**The pin:** `setup_post_options::smoothing_follows_each_ops_own_setup_not_the_active_one` uses two setups: Setup1 has smoothing on, and Setup2 follows the document's off. Exactly one op asks for smoothing, with either setup active.\n- I swapped the old `post_options(world)` gate back in and the test fails at line 333, so it pins the fix.\n- It passes with the fix.\n\n**Gate (trial merge with upstream/main, clean):**\n- `setup_post_options` 10, `smoothing` 6, `posting` 17, `tormach_post` 10, `project_roundtrip` 71: all green.\n- clippy `-D warnings` on the app lib and `setup_post_options`: clean.\n\n**Non-blocking:** the document-wide `Smoothing` word in `options_value` still reports the active setup's choice. That's fine for scripts, but its doc comment could say so.\n\nRequested changes: none. The needs-rework stood on d4f3145a; this head is a new push that fixes it.",
